C03: a Steam download, install or uninstall request first reads the library entitlement of the named game (INSTALL1617)

Fifteen open survey rows ask BAXY to download, install or uninstall a named game in Steam. The product could only attempt the installation effect, which fails closed without an entitlement (steam_entitlement_not_verified), and the mind did not resolve those requests at all. A read-only operation, game.entitlement.named(title), now answers whether the title is in the person's authenticated Steam library (closed title table or the local snapshot; librarycache entitlement) and whether it is installed (appmanifest), without downloading, purchasing or opening any dialog. The mind decides that read for «descarga/instala/desinstala X en steam» (also «seam», «de steam», «Necesito que instalaes …») with the person's own spelling of the title, and the composer states the observed consequence — not in the library, so it cannot be downloaded or installed; not installed, for an uninstall; already installed — the failure lens treating that consequence as the observed state, not as a failed read. Registry-wide diff: 16 literals now decide game.entitlement.named; every other literal unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


